{%- macro table(tbl, compact=False) -%}
<div class="table-wrap">
<table class="data{{ ' compact' if compact }}">
  <thead><tr>
  {%- for h in tbl.headers %}
    <th class="{{ 'num' if loop.index0 >= tbl.numeric_from }}">{{ h }}</th>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in tbl.rows %}
    <tr>
    {%- for c in row %}
      <td class="{{ 'num' if loop.index0 >= tbl.numeric_from or c.numeric }} {{ c.style }}">{{ c.text }}</td>
    {%- endfor %}
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{%- if tbl.caption %}<p class="caption">{{ tbl.caption }}</p>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="generator" content="engmech {{ version }}">
<title>{{ title }}</title>
<style>
{% include "style.css" %}
</style>
{% if plotly_js %}<script>{{ plotly_js }}</script>
{% else %}<script src="https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-2.35.2.min.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
{% endif %}
<script>
{% include "figure.js" %}
</script>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header class="page masthead">
  <div class="masthead-text">
    <p class="eyebrow">Rigid-body analysis report</p>
    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if lead %}<div class="lede"><p>{{ lead }}</p></div>{% endif %}
    <ul class="chips">{% for f in facts %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    <div class="meta">
      {% if source %}Model <code>{{ source }}</code> · {% endif %}Generated {{ generated }} · engmech {{ version }}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% if logo %}<img class="logo" src="{{ logo.data_uri }}" alt="Logo">{% endif %}
</header>

<section class="card" id="summary">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Summary</h2></div>
  <div class="statuses">
  {% set good = cases | selectattr('style', 'equalto', 'good') | list %}
  {% if multi and good | length > 1 %}
  <div class="status good">
    <span class="mark">✓</span>
    <span class="text"><strong>Equilibrium verified for {{ 'all ' if good | length == cases | length }}{{ good | length }} load cases and combinations</strong>
      <span class="case">{{ good | map(attribute='name') | join(', ') }} · max relative residual {{ '%.0e' | format(good | map(attribute='case.max_residual') | max) }}</span>
    </span>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% for c in cases if not (multi and good | length > 1 and c.style == 'good') %}
  <div class="status {{ c.style }}">
    <span class="mark">{{ {'good': '✓', 'warn': '!', 'bad': '✗'}[c.style] }}</span>
    <span class="text"><strong>{{ c.headline }}</strong>
      {% if multi %}<span class="case">{{ 'Combination' if c.case.kind == 'combination' else 'Load case' }} <em>{{ c.name }}</em></span>{% endif %}
    </span>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if results.sensitivity %}
  <div class="status warn">
    <span class="mark">!</span>
    <span class="text"><strong>Results are sensitive to geometry</strong>{{ results.sensitivity }}</span>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if checks %}
  {% set failed = results.checks | rejectattr('passed') | list %}
  <div class="status {{ 'bad' if failed else 'good' }}">
    <span class="mark">{{ '✗' if failed else '✓' }}</span>
    <span class="text"><strong>{{ results.checks | length - failed | length }} of {{ results.checks | length }} checks passed</strong></span>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if notes or mechanism %}
  <ul class="summary-notes">
    {% for n in notes %}<li>{{ n }}</li>{% endfor %}
    {% for mode in mechanism %}<li>Free motion: {{ mode | join('; ') }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}
</section>

{% if envelope %}
<section class="card" id="cases">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Load cases compared</h2>
    <nav class="sub jump">Details:
      {% for c in cases %}<a href="#case-{{ loop.index }}">{{ c.name }}</a>{{ " · " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}
    </nav>
  </div>
  {% for tbl in envelope %}
  <h3>{{ tbl.title }}{% if tbl.units %} <span class="units">{{ tbl.units }}</span>{% endif %}</h3>
  {{ table(tbl) }}
  {% endfor %}
</section>
{% endif %}

{% for c in cases %}
<section class="card" id="case-{{ loop.index }}">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>{% if multi %}{{ 'Combination' if c.case.kind == 'combination' else 'Load case' }}: {{ c.name }}{% else %}Results{% endif %}</h2>
    {% if c.case.kind == 'combination' %}<span class="sub">{{ c.factors }}</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if c.case.warnings %}
  <ul class="warnings {{ 'bad' if c.case.status == 'unbalanced' else 'warn' }}">
    {% for w in c.case.warnings %}<li>{{ w }}</li>{% endfor %}
    {% for mode in c.excited %}<li>Free motion driven by the loads: {{ mode | join('; ') }}</li>{% endfor %}
    {% for r in c.redundancy %}<li>Self-stress state (can be added in any amount): {{ r }}</li>{% endfor %}
    {% if c.redundancy %}<li>Arrows marked * show only the components that equilibrium determines.</li>{% endif %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% for tbl in c.tables %}
  <h3>{{ tbl.title }}{% if tbl.units %} <span class="units">{{ tbl.units }}</span>{% endif %}</h3>
  {{ table(tbl) }}
  {% endfor %}
  <h3>Free-body diagram</h3>
  <div class="figure" id="figure-{{ loop.index }}">
    <div class="views" hidden></div>
    <div class="plot" id="fig-{{ loop.index }}"></div>
    <div class="print-views"></div>
  </div>
  <script>engmechFigure("figure-{{ loop.index }}", {{ c.figure }}, {{ (title ~ ' ' ~ c.name) | tojson }});</script>
  <details{% if not c.case.verified %} open{% endif %}>
    <summary>Equilibrium verification</summary>
    <div class="body">
    {% for tbl in c.verification %}
    <h3>{{ tbl.title }}</h3>
    {{ table(tbl, compact=True) }}
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Applied loads{% if multi %} in this {{ 'combination' if c.case.kind == 'combination' else 'case' }}{% endif %}</summary>
    <div class="body">{{ table(c.loads, compact=True) }}</div>
  </details>
</section>
{% endfor %}

{% if checks %}
<section class="card" id="checks">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Checks</h2></div>
  {{ table(checks) }}
</section>
{% endif %}

{% if notes_text %}
<section class="card" id="notes">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Notes</h2><span class="sub">from the model description</span></div>
  <div class="notes">
  {% for kind, text in notes_text %}{% if kind == 'pre' %}<pre>{{ text }}</pre>{% else %}<p>{{ text }}</p>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="card" id="model">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Model</h2></div>
  <div class="grid-2">
    <dl class="facts">
      {% for k, v in determinacy %}<dt>{{ k }}</dt><dd>{{ v }}</dd>{% endfor %}
    </dl>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Length</dt><dd>{{ units.label('length') }}</dd>
      <dt>Force</dt><dd>{{ units.label('force') }}</dd>
      <dt>Moment</dt><dd>{{ units.label('moment') }}</dd>
      <dt>Mass</dt><dd>{{ units.label('mass') }}</dd>
      {% if gravity %}<dt>Gravity</dt><dd>{{ gravity }}</dd>{% endif %}
    </dl>
  </div>
  {% if definitions %}<h3>{{ definitions.title }}</h3>{{ table(definitions) }}{% endif %}
  {% if mass %}
  <h3>{{ mass.title }} <span class="units">{{ mass.units }}</span></h3>
  {{ table(mass) }}
  <details>
    <summary>Inertia tensors and principal axes</summary>
    <div class="body grid-2">
    {% for name, d in inertia.items() %}
      <div class="inertia">
        <h4>{{ name }}</h4>
        <div class="label">Inertia about the centre of gravity, global axes ({{ inertia_unit }})</div>
        <table class="matrix">{% for row in d.tensor %}<tr>{% for x in row %}<td>{{ x }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</table>
        <div class="label">Principal moments ({{ inertia_unit }}) and axes</div>
        <table class="matrix">{% for i in range(3) %}<tr><td>{{ d.moments[i] }}</td><td>[{{ d.axes[i] | join(', ') }}]</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table>
        <div class="label">Radii of gyration</div>
        <div>{{ d.radii | join(', ') }}</div>
        {% if d.shapes | length > 1 %}
        <div class="label">Parts</div>
        <table class="matrix">{% for label, m, cog in d.shapes %}<tr><td style="text-align:left">{{ label }}</td><td>{{ m }}</td><td>({{ cog }})</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </details>
  {% endif %}
  {% if points or parameters %}
  <div class="grid-2">
    {% if points %}<div><h3>{{ points.title }}</h3>{{ table(points, compact=True) }}</div>{% endif %}
    {% if parameters %}<div><h3>{{ parameters.title }}</h3>{{ table(parameters, compact=True) }}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="card" id="provenance">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Provenance</h2><span class="sub">what produced these results</span></div>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>engmech</dt><dd>{{ provenance.engmech }}</dd>
    <dt>Generated</dt><dd>{{ provenance.generated.replace('T', ' ').replace('+00:00', '') }} UTC</dd>
    <dt>Python / platform</dt><dd>{{ provenance.python }} on {{ provenance.platform }}</dd>
    <dt>Libraries</dt><dd>{% for k, v in provenance.libraries.items() %}{{ k }} {{ v }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</dd>
    {% if provenance.input %}
    <dt>Input file</dt><dd><code>{{ provenance.input.path }}</code> ({{ provenance.input.bytes }} bytes)</dd>
    <dt>SHA-256</dt><dd><code class="hash">{{ provenance.input.sha256 }}</code></dd>
    {% endif %}
    {% if provenance.parameter_overrides %}
    <dt>Parameter overrides</dt><dd>{% for k, v in provenance.parameter_overrides.items() %}<code>{{ k }} = {{ v }}</code>{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</dd>
    {% endif %}
  </dl>
  {% if source_text %}
  <details>
    <summary>Input file as analysed</summary>
    <div class="body"><pre class="source">{{ source_text }}</pre></div>
  </details>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="card method" id="method">
  <div class="section-head"><h2>Method and conventions</h2></div>
  <p>Every body is rigid. Unknowns are the force and moment components each support or joint can transmit; the equations are force and moment equilibrium of every body{% if planar %} in the xy-plane (ΣFx = ΣFy = ΣMz = 0){% endif %}. Prescribed motion adds d'Alembert inertial loads, −m·a at the centre of gravity and −(I·α + ω × I·ω), which turns the same equations into Newton-Euler dynamics.</p>
  <p>Reactions are the force and moment <em>on the body</em> from the ground, at the support point, in global axes. Joint forces are reported on the "On" body from the "From" body (for <code>bodies: [a, b]</code>, on b from a); the other body receives the opposite. N is a normal force, positive when pushing on the body; T is an axial force, positive in tension.</p>
  <p>Before solving, the equations are scaled by the model size so that stability and determinacy do not depend on the length unit. Loads that do work on a free motion (a mechanism) are reported as out of equilibrium. Components that cannot be found from equilibrium alone are reported as indeterminate rather than guessed; when joint stiffnesses are given, redundant forces are shared by least work.</p>
  <p>The equilibrium verification sums every load and joint force on each body directly, independent of the solver, and must close to a relative residual below 10⁻⁶.</p>
</section>
<footer>engmech {{ version }} · {{ generated }}</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
